course: dictionary
lesson: 15969
title: Unwillingness and the word beginning un-
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unwillingness is a noun. It means not wanting to do something. It comes from willing, which means ready and happy to do something, with un- added to show "not". So unwillingness is the feeling of not being willing.
explain: «Sam showed his unwillingness to help by folding his arms and looking away.» Sam's arms and looking away tell you he did not want to help. You can check the meaning by swapping in "not wanting to": Sam showed his not wanting to help. It still makes sense.
explain: Unwillingness is usually followed by to and a doing word, such as to try or to share. «Mia's unwillingness to try the new game kept her on the bench.» The phrase unwillingness to tells you what the person does not want to do.
fact: Unwillingness means not wanting to do something.
fact: The prefix un- means "not", so unwillingness is the opposite of willingness.
fact: Unwillingness is uncountable, so it has no plural. You do not say "unwillingnesses".
fact: The phrase «unwillingness to» is followed by a doing word, as in «unwillingness to try».
fact: In a story, a character's unwillingness to help may change later on.
exercise: «Tom's unwillingness to share his crayons made the table quiet.» What does unwillingness mean? | A kind of paint | *Not wanting to do something | Being very happy to help | Losing something by accident
exercise: Which word means the opposite of unwillingness? | *Willingness | Tiredness | Sadness | Carelessness
exercise: «Mia showed an unwillingness to try the new game, so she sat and watched.» What does this suggest about Mia? | She had forgotten the rules | She was very excited to play | *She did not want to play | She had already won the game
test: Which word means not wanting to do something? | Playfulness | Generosity | *Unwillingness
test: Which word completes the phrase: unwillingness ___ try? | for | at | *to | on
exam: Which sentence uses unwillingness correctly? | The unwillingness sang a song loudly. | The dog ran unwillingness to the park. | *The boy's unwillingness to tidy his room worried his mum.
